# ==============================================================================
# Direct & Unlimited Image Sources (NO API KEY REQUIRED / 100% FREE)
# ==============================================================================
# 1. Wikimedia Commons:
#    Endpoint: https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/api.php
#    Usage: Unlimited authentic 4K/8K photos for Indian monuments, temples, waterfalls.
#
# 2. Flickr Creative Commons Travel Streams:
#    Endpoint: https://api.flickr.com/services/feeds/photos_public.gne
#    Usage: Unlimited authentic street & travel photography in 2K/4K resolution.
#
# 3. The Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met Open Access):
#    Endpoint: https://collectionapi.metmuseum.org/public/collection/v1/
#    Usage: Unlimited historical 4K photography & artwork of Indian palaces, forts, Mughal/Rajput architecture.
#
# 4. Art Institute of Chicago (AIC IIIF 4K API):
#    Endpoint: https://api.artic.edu/api/v1/artworks/search
#    Usage: Unlimited dynamic 3840px 4K IIIF generator for Indian heritage architecture.
#
# 5. Openverse Public Search:
#    Endpoint: https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/?q={query}
#    Usage: Over 700 million Creative Commons images.
#
# 6. Cleveland Museum of Art (CMA Open Access):
#    Endpoint: https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks
#    Usage: Unlimited 3400px+ Ultra HD CC0 photography of Indian royal palaces, forts, temples.
#
# 7. Victoria and Albert Museum (V&A IIIF 2K/4K API):
#    Endpoint: https://api.vam.ac.uk/v2/objects/search
#    Usage: Unlimited 2048px IIIF photography of Indian historical architecture & temples.
#
# 8. NASA Earth & Satellite Imagery:
#    Endpoint: https://images-api.nasa.gov/search
#    Usage: Unlimited Ultra-HD satellite vistas of the Himalayas, rivers, coasts, and landscapes.
